    "heading": "remove-mdx-componentstsx",
    "content": "mdx-components.tsx is no longer used. It now allows only MDX components passed from MDX body's components prop."
  }, {
    "heading": "remove-mdx-componentstsx",
    "content": "This encourages explicit import of MDX components."
  }, {
    "heading": "remove-mdx-componentstsx",
    "content": "Previously, mdx-components.tsx worked by injecting an import to every compiled Markdown/MDX file.\nIt's somewhat unnecessary because you can always import the components explicitly, or replace default HTML tags like img from MDX body's components prop."
  }, {
    "heading": "define-collections",
    "content": "Collection is now introduced on source config file (source.config.ts).\nIt refers to a collection of files/content, such as Markdown files or JSON/YAML files."
  }, {
    "heading": "define-collections",
    "content": "Every collection has its own config, you can have customised Zod schema to validate its data, or collection-level MDX options for content collections."
  }, {
    "heading": "define-collections",
    "content": "You can create a source config file, and add the following:"
  }, {
    "heading": "define-collections",
    "content": "defineDocs declares two collections, one with doc type that scans content files (e.g. md/mdx), one with meta type that scans meta files (e.g. json)."
  }, {
    "heading": "define-collections",
    "content": "Now you can generate types using fumadocs-mdx command, it's recommended to set it as a postinstall script."
  }, {
    "heading": "define-collections",
    "content": "When starting the development server, a .source folder will be generated, it contains all parsed collections/files.\nYou can add it to .gitignore, it will replace the old .map file."
  }, {
    "heading": "define-collections",
    "content": "To access the collections, import them from the folder with their original name in source.config.ts."
  }, {
    "heading": "define-collections",
    "content": "Now to integrate it with Fumadocs framework, change your source.ts from:"
  }, {
    "heading": "define-collections",
    "content": "to:"
  }, {
    "heading": "define-collections",
    "content": "we now recommend exporting the output of loader directly as a single variable."
  }, {
    "heading": "define-collections",
    "content": "schema option is no longer defined in source.ts, it's handled by source.config.ts."
  }, {
    "heading": "define-collections",
    "content": "it takes two collections: docs (content) and meta (meta.json).\nYou can leave meta as an empty array if it is unused, so you can define only a collection for docs."
  }, {
    "heading": "pagedata",
    "content": "When using with loader, you no longer need data.frontmatter to access frontmatter data.\nIt is merged into the page.data object."
  }, {
    "heading": "mdx-options",
    "content": "Instead of passing them to next.config file, define a global config in source.config.ts:"
  }, {
    "heading": "collection-schema",
    "content": "The schema option of collection allow you to customise the validation schema, it accepts a Zod type."
  }, {
    "heading": "collection-schema",
    "content": "For defineDocs, see schema."
  }, {
    "heading": "multiple-types",
    "content": "Same as before, you can call loader multiple times for different types (e.g. for docs and blog)."
  }, {
    "heading": "multiple-types",
    "content": "and the corresponding source.config.ts:"
